      "typeVersion": 4.5,
      "position": [
        1100,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Why .item, not .first()\nBuild message's input is Find customer, so $json is the customer. The order is reached with $('Orders').item, which follows the item link back to *this* customer's order. .first() would give every message item 0's data.\n\nFind customer has **Always Output Data** on (Settings), so an order whose customer_id has no match still produces a message (\"Hello Customer\") instead of vanishing.\n\nStep through items 0, 1 and 2 in the Input panel: each preview must show a different customer.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 420
      },
      "id": "9e1deaba-5690-40ea-af05-cc30c95ad52f",
      "name": "Item linking",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        550,
        144
      ]
    }
  ],
